BalanceNG 3.419 is now available athttp://www.BalanceNG.net
Release-Date: November 10, 2012

----

Changes:

IPv6 Neighbor Solicitation messages are now properly sent to the solicited-node multicast address according to RFC-4861 and RFC-4291. Before, they had been sent wrongly to the unicast IPv6 address, which made some devices not to respond to those messages. Updating is recommended if BNG is deployed in IPv6 environments.

Download-URL:
https://www.inlab.de/balanceng/download.html

----

About BalanceNG:

BalanceNG is an IPv6 capable software load-balancer and runs on Linux and Solaris operating systems.

About Inlab Software GmbH:

Inlab Software GmbH, founded in 1991 is an ISV (Independent Software Vendor) located in Gruenwald near Munich, Germany. Inlab focuses on networking system software, load-balancing software, programming languages and security software. Inlab develops software for Linux and Solaris operating systems and develops both commercial products and Open-Source software.

----

OEM-Partner BalanceNG certified systems:

* Available Worldwide:
   The SECUDOS Load-Balancer (SLB) Product Family
   distributed by LANDITEC
   http://www.landitec.com/SECUDOS-Load-Balancer:::52.html

